cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact HINC-001 release or DOI when available. Before release, cite
  the paper identifier and exact source commit.
title: Hidden Infinitesimal Noncommutativity in Endomorphism Monoids of Two Graded Gerstenhaber Algebras
type: article
version: 0.1.0-candidate
authors:
  - family-names: Novak
    given-names: Matthew S.
abstract: >-
  We classify candidate strict graded Gerstenhaber endomorphism monoid schemes
  for two explicit characteristic-two subalgebras of the Hochschild cohomology
  of the dual numbers. The two monoids share a reduced crossing core but differ
  by an infinitesimal skew thickening and a clopen unit doubling. A bounded
  algebraic kernel and the principal coefficient classifications are publicly
  proof-assistant verified; the complete scheme-level manuscript remains under
  specialist and historical-equivalence review.
repository-code: https://github.com/novakprotocol/N-Human-AI-Mathematics
keywords:
  - algebraic monoids
  - Gerstenhaber algebra
  - Hochschild cohomology
  - nonreduced schemes
  - formal verification
  - human-AI mathematics
